/-!
# The `q`-expansions of `Sm1Ref` and of `KPlusSumRef` (the `K₊` reference coefficient list)

`KPlusSumRef = Sm1Ref + … + Sm5Ref` is the reference part of the `K₊`-group of the
`Sh`-cleared `d = 24` bracket (`KPlus24Group = -(c z² KPlusSumRef) + dKPlus24`), and every
`Sm_iRef` is an explicit polynomial in `q = qParamFun z` with `τ`-atom coefficients
(`Sm2Ref_qexp`, `Sm3Ref_qexp`, `Sm4Ref_qexp`, `Sm5Ref_q1`).  This module supplies the missing
`Sm1Ref` expansion (degrees `1`–`12`, from `Sm1Ref_qform` + the definition of `W0q`), and
then *sums* the five into the full coefficient list of `KPlusSumRef`.

Consequences for the `E(z)`-expansion of the bracket: `KPlus24Ref = -(c z² KPlusSumRef)` is
*even* in `E = Ept z`, so its `E^{2m}`-coefficient is `-(c z²)` times the `q^m`-coefficient
of `KPlusSumRef`; in particular (cf. `KPlusQ1`, which *is* the `q¹`-coefficient by
construction) the `E²`-coefficient of the `K₊` reference is `-(c z²) KPlusQ1`.
-/

